4. Public Customer Creation Flow
This is the simplest flow, showing an open endpoint for public user registration.

@startuml
title 4. Public Customer Creation Flow

actor "Client (Guest)" as Client
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "User Service\n(Spring Boot)" as Service
database "Database" as DB

skinparam sequenceActorStyle awesome

== Create Customer Request ==

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/users/customer\nBody: {firstName, ..., password}
Gateway -> Service: Forward Request
activate Service

Service -> Service: Perform validations\n(e.g., email format, password strength)
Service -> Service: Hash password
Service -> DB: INSERT INTO users (..., role='CUSTOMER')
activate DB
DB --> Service: User Created
deactivate DB

Service --> Gateway: **201 Created**
Gateway --> Client: Return 201 Created response
deactivate Service

@enduml